      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately it\u0027s not that easy; there are 3 possible values for these fields: 0, 1, 2 (i.e. BASE, ONELEVEL and SUBTREE). [1]\n\nI agree about exposing implementation details though. \n\nDo you think implementing something like register_enum would be a good idea? Or just using some predefined strings like \u0027base\u0027, \u0027onelevel\u0027 and \u0027subtree\u0027 and then checking them in BaseLdap\u0027s constructor?\n\n[1] http://www.python-ldap.org/doc/html/ldapurl.html?highlight\u003dscope#constants",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAM3//A5E\u003d",
      "revId": "11a46aeebdc54f21a37b3b5394ea256c92c96d98",
